1. Problem Statement
Many households use different electrical appliances every day, but they usually don't know which appliance is consuming more electricity or where most of their electricity is actually being used. Because of this, it becomes difficult to control unnecessary usage and also manage the monthly electricity bill. The proposed system estimates the electricity consumption and cost of individual appliances, finds the appliances with higher usage, checks the consumption against the monthly budget, and gives simple personalized suggestions on where the user can reduce electricity usage and save money.
2. Objectives
The main objectives of this project are:
To develop a simple Java based electricity consumption advisor.
To calculate monthly energy consumption of household appliances.
To estimate the monthly electricity bill.
To rank appliances according to their electricity consumption.
To identify the major sources of energy consumption.
To compare estimated electricity expenses with the user's budget.
To generate recommendations for reducing electricity usage.
To encourage better awareness about household electricity consumption.
3. Proposed System
The user provides the monthly electricity budget and electricity rate. Appliance information such as appliance name, wattage and daily usage is then processed by the system.
The system calculates the monthly energy consumption using the appliance power rating and its average daily operating time.
The basic formula used is:
Monthly Energy Consumption = (Wattage × Daily Usage × 30) / 1000
The result is obtained in kWh, which is commonly referred to as a unit of electricity.
After calculating the consumption of every appliance, the system calculates the estimated electricity cost.
Estimated Cost = Total Energy Consumption × Cost per Unit
The appliances are then sorted from highest to lowest consumption. The system also checks whether the estimated bill has crossed the user's monthly budget.
