8. Algorithm
Step 1
Start the program.
Step 2
Enter the monthly electricity budget.
Step 3
Enter the electricity cost per unit.
Step 4
Add household appliance information.
Step 5
For each appliance, calculate:
Monthly Units =
(Wattage × Daily Hours × 30) / 1000

Step 6
Calculate the cost of each appliance.
Monthly Cost = Monthly Units × Rate per Unit

Step 7
Add the consumption of all appliances to find total monthly consumption.
Step 8
Add the individual appliance costs to obtain the estimated monthly bill.
Step 9
Sort the appliances according to their monthly energy consumption.
Step 10
Identify appliances having a comparatively high contribution to total consumption.
Step 11
Compare the estimated bill with the monthly budget.
Step 12
If the bill is higher than the budget, display a budget alert.
Step 13
Generate energy-saving recommendations for high-consuming appliances.
Step 14
Display the complete analysis and terminate the program.
9. Working of the Project
Suppose a household has a fan with a power rating of 75 watts and it is used for 8 hours every day.
The monthly consumption is:
= (75 × 8 × 30) / 1000
= 18 kWh

If the electricity rate is Rs 8 per unit:
Cost = 18 × 8
     = Rs 144

The same calculation is performed for all the appliances.
For example, if the household has an air conditioner rated at 1500 W and it is used for 6 hours per day:
= (1500 × 6 × 30) / 1000
= 270 kWh

So, in this example, the air conditioner consumes much more electricity than the fan.
The system identifies this difference and considers the air conditioner as one of the major sources of consumption.
10. Main Features
10.1 Appliance Consumption Calculation
The system calculates the approximate monthly electricity consumption of every appliance separately.
10.2 Estimated Electricity Bill
After finding total energy consumption, the program calculates the expected electricity cost using the given rate per unit.
10.3 Appliance Ranking
The appliances are sorted according to their energy consumption. The appliance consuming the highest amount is shown at the top.
10.4 Budget Comparison
The user can enter a monthly budget. The system compares this amount with the estimated bill.
If:
Estimated Bill > Budget

the system displays a budget warning.
10.5 Major Consumption Identification
The program calculates the percentage contribution of appliances to total electricity consumption. Appliances contributing significantly are considered major sources.
10.6 Saving Recommendations
For high-consuming appliances, the system gives suggestions such as reducing unnecessary operating hours, switching appliances off when not required and considering energy-efficient alternatives.

11. Limitations
The current version has some limitations.
The calculation is based on the wattage and average daily usage entered into the program.
Appliance efficiency and standby consumption are not considered in detail.
Recommendations are mainly rule-based.
The current implementation does not use a trained machine learning model for prediction.
It is currently a console application and does not have a graphical user interface.

12. Future Scope
The project can be improved in several ways in the future.
Machine Learning Prediction
Historical electricity consumption data can be used to train a machine learning model to predict future electricity consumption.
Dynamic Tariff Calculation
Different electricity tariff slabs can be included so that the estimated bill becomes closer to an actual electricity bill.
Mobile or Web Application
A graphical interface can be developed so that normal users can view their consumption through charts and dashboards.
